{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Done. Verified: on `main` at `defab1d` with the fix merged, working tree clean, 91/91 tests, `dist/` rebuilt — so your global `tb`/`turnbridge` now runs the fixed adapter.\n\n**`../turnbridge-worktrees/` created**, with a README recording the convention:\n\n```\ncd ../turnbridge\ngit worktree add ../turnbridge-worktrees/<branch> -b <branch>\ncd ../turnbridge-worktrees/<branch> && npm install && npm run build\n```\n\nTwo gotchas I wrote into that README, because both would bite silently:\n\n1. **Each worktree needs its own `npm install`.** `conversation-ledger` is a `file:` dependency resolved relative to the checkout, and `node_modules/` isn't shared. A fresh worktree won't build without it.\n2. **The global `tb` is npm-linked to the main checkout, not to your worktree.** So `tb` always runs `../turnbridge/dist`, whatever branch that directory is on. To exercise a worktree's build, run its own `node dist/cli.js`.\n\nThat second point is actually the argument for this whole convention, and it bit us today: the opencode fix lived on a branch inside the main checkout, so your `tb` was fixed only while that branch happened to be checked out — and would have silently reverted the moment anyone ran `git checkout main`. Worktrees make that impossible. I've saved the convention to project memory so future sessions follow it.\n\nAlso cleaned up: both merged local branches deleted (`-d`, so it would have refused anything unmerged), leaving only `main`.\n\n**One thing left for you:** the remote branches `origin/docs/fabrication-tiers-and-opencode-provider-bug` and `origin/fix/opencode-continuation` still exist — the merges didn't delete them, which is what caused the #8 retarget problem in the first place. Both are fully merged into main, so they're safe to remove, but that's a remote-side deletion I'd rather you authorize:\n\n```\ngit push origin --delete docs/fabrication-tiers-and-opencode-provider-bug fix/opencode-continuation\ngit remote prune origin\n```\n\nStill open from earlier: the two opencode probes, and codex 0.147.0 drift.\n\nresult: On main at `defab1d` with the opencode fix merged and rebuilt (91/91 tests, global `tb` now runs fixed code), `../turnbridge-worktrees/` created with a README covering the per-worktree `npm install` and npm-link gotchas, merged local branches cleaned up — two merged remote branches left for you to delete.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"defab1d48ffb334ef077b543c74110f5a05efd71","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","seq":1137},"id":"ev1-626699d7c86fed56b26098dc1193f8f419d8697211aaef3971c0b5dc65a65bb3","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-12T00:33:20.500Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.228","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"Done. Verified: on `main` at `defab1d` with the fix merged, working tree clean, 91/91 tests, `dist/` rebuilt — so your global `tb`/`turnbridge` now runs the fixed adapter.\n\n**`../turnbridge-worktrees/` created**, with a README recording the convention:\n\n```\ncd ../turnbridge\ngit worktree add ../turnbridge-worktrees/<branch> -b <branch>\ncd ../turnbridge-worktrees/<branch> && npm install && npm run build\n```\n\nTwo gotchas I wrote into that README, because both would bite silently:\n\n1. **Each worktree needs its own `npm install`.** `conversation-ledger` is a `file:` dependency resolved relative to the checkout, and `node_modules/` isn't shared. A fresh worktree won't build without it.\n2. **The global `tb` is npm-linked to the